## Why choose a refurbished business laptop

Business laptops are engineered for the way people actually work: carried every day, used for eight or more hours, and expected to last several years. That's why they make some of the best-value refurbished computers you can buy.

### Built to last

Compared with consumer laptops at a similar spec, business models typically have stiffer chassis, stronger hinges and keyboards designed for heavy typing — often spill-resistant. Manufacturers state that many are tested against MIL-STD-810 methods for durability.

### Secure by design

A TPM security chip is standard, and many models add fingerprint readers, IR cameras for Windows Hello, webcam privacy shutters or smart-card readers. Some HP EliteBooks include a built-in privacy screen.

### Easy to service and upgrade

Memory, storage and batteries are often straightforward to replace, and spare parts remain available long after the laptop's launch. That means a refurbished business laptop can be kept running — and upgraded — for years.

### Choosing between the big three

- **[Lenovo ThinkPad](/brand/lenovo)** — best-in-class keyboards and the TrackPoint. T series for all-round use, X1 Carbon for travel.
- **[Dell Latitude](/brand/dell)** — reliable all-rounders. The 5000 series offers great value; the 7000 series is lighter and more premium.
- **[HP EliteBook](/brand/hp)** — slim, polished designs with strong security features. The EliteBook 840 is the most popular model.

Read our full comparison: [Latitude vs ThinkPad vs EliteBook](/blog/best-business-laptops-for-professionals).

### Recommended configuration

For most office work, look for an **8th generation or newer Intel Core i5**, **8–16GB of RAM**, a **256GB or larger SSD** and a **Full HD screen**. Many laptops matching that description are available [under ₹30,000](/laptops/under-30000).

